		{
			description: [
				"When the machine mode is switched while the machine is running, the machine will try to continue running the recipe before the switch. Only by reshaping or refreshing the input material can the machine change the operating mode."
				""
				"Example 1: A large fractional distillation plant runs the distilled water recipe in distillation column mode. The distillation column recipe is still executed after switching to distillation chamber mode."
				""
				"Example 2: A large brewery runs the potato + water → biomass formula in brewing room mode. After switching to fermenter mode, it will not switch to the potato → poisonous potato formula."
				""
				"Example 3: When the space elevator acquisition module runs the mining recipe, it switches to the mining fluid mode and still mines."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"In JEI, you will find that the tooltip of some probability-related materials/products has \\\"voltage bonus: +n%/per level\\\", where the specific value of \\\"per level\\\" is the maximum recipe voltage level of the machine itself minus the minimum voltage level of the recipe itself."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"In JEI, you will find that the tooltip of some probability-related materials/products has \"voltage bonus: +n%/per level\", where the specific value of \"per level\" is the maximum recipe voltage level of the machine itself minus the minimum voltage level of the recipe itself."
			]
